        "date": "2026-11-07T23:17:39Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion,app): turning kinds approach and rough from the setup stock\n\nProfile rough and finish, groove rough and finish, parting, threading and\nform now read the revolved stock envelope (the bar's widest radius about\nthe part's fitted axis, StockEnv), passed in from the app layer the way\nthe meridian rapid law reads the stock. In a bar wider than the part:\n\n- every approach and retract stands clear of the bar's OD by a 1 mm\n  radial clearance (an insert's nose added);\n- the profile rough's ladder counts its rungs from the bar's OD down to\n  the part plus stock-to-leave, dropping rungs that never reach under\n  the OD; groove rough and parting peck down from the OD.\n\nA 20 mm bar roughed to a 12 mm part now generates passes from r 10 down\nand posts clean, where #103's law refused it with RapidInStock. A bar\nno wider than the part (every lathe golden) keeps the part-based program\nunchanged; no readable stock keeps it too and names that in a path note.\nFacing (#122), the contour rides and boring are not changed. Parting\nmoves from blade.rs to parting.rs for the size budget; turning_profile's\nfixture moves from a 40 mm box to bar-sized stock.\n\nFixes #130\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
